{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input-output conv path when none exists gives large gains, whereas replacing an existing skip/pool/1x1 op on edge 3 is roughly neutral or negative."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual shortcut added where no direct path existed strongly helps optimization, far more than swapping out an existing conv on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 also missing, removing edge 3 leaves only the deep path through node 2, producing the largest observed accuracy drops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, edge 5 is the main route from intermediate nodes to the output, so cutting it can nearly disconnect the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input-output edge, edge 5 carries more of the output signal and removing it hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 3 is absent the path through node 1 becomes critical, so removing edge 0 causes much larger drops."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 3 is none, edge 4's skip acts as the shortcut, and converting it to a conv hurts trainability."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Skip-heavy cells lack learnable capacity, so introducing a 3x3 conv yields far larger gains than in conv-rich cells."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge"